<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Regeneration (Colombia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880s–<a href="/years/1900">1900</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Regeneration was the political movement led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rafael-nunez">Rafael Núñez</a> in Colombia from the 1880s that replaced the federal, liberal order of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> of Colombia with a centralised state. Backed by Conservatives and moderate Liberals, it produced the Constitution of 1886, which created the Republic of Colombia, strengthened the presidency and restored the Catholic Church's role in education. Liberal opposition to its rule led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thousand-days-war">Thousand Days' War</a> of 1899–1902.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/regeneration-colombia.jpg" alt="Regeneration (Colombia)" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Darío Gaitán · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Monstruo,_La_Regeneraci%C3%B3n_by_Dar%C3%ADo_Gait%C3%A1n_(1870-1904).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
